  "limitations": [
    "Loopback functional drill; no production RPO/RTO or power-loss claim.",
    "The legacy archive is produced by the trusted format19 binary and is never edited.",
    "source_head values are repository heads, not binary build provenance.",
    "A source older than a ledger schema gains that ledger empty (except an exact settled-migration seed); a genuine source that already carries schema139/140/141/142 rows has the exact rows preserved across migration143, never fabricated.",
    "A genuine pre-schema140 source gains an empty migration-140 snapshot/pin schema; a genuine source that carries it has its exact rows preserved and every old snapshot left metadata-only.",
    "The schema141 ledger tables are derived from the generated 140-vs-139 catalogs; a source older than schema141 must leave them at the exact settled seed, while a genuine format16/17/18 source's rows are compared exactly. This fixture inserts no hold, request or consumption row.",
    "The schema142 pack-registration/membership/history/usage tables are derived from the generated 142-vs-141 catalogs and must stay empty on a genuine pre-142 source, while a genuine format18 A4 source's rows and gate mode are preserved exactly. This fixture inserts no pack row and claims no pack-verified gate.",
    "The schema143 pack-snapshot binding/history/permanent-usage tables are derived from the generated 143-vs-142 catalogs and must stay empty; no A5 pack snapshot, pin or history row is fabricated and no complete Git-read snapshot is claimed.",
    "The format18/schema142 drill seeds its genuine A4 S3/native-Git pack/A3 ledger with the retained old A4 helper (seed mode only) before the old archive is written; that helper's verify mode is never run against the schema143 target.",
    "A format16 drill requires root to supply the genuine retained old schema140 producer and its archive; format17/18 drills require the genuine retained schema141/schema142 producers (the format18 producer is the retained A4 app); this harness never fabricates or relabels one."
  ],
